You are acting as a senior software architect, React engineer, QA automation engineer, frontend security reviewer, accessibility specialist, and performance engineer.

Your task is to perform a complete technical audit and final refinement of my existing Online Voting System (OVS) project.

This is Phase 7, the final major development phase.

Your objective is to ensure that all functionality implemented in Phases 1–6 works correctly together.

Do not simply perform a visual review.

Inspect the actual source code, run the application, execute automated tests, identify defects, fix them, and verify the fixes.

Work directly on the existing project.

Do not create a new application.

Do not unnecessarily rewrite working modules.

Do not introduce a backend.

All functionality must remain frontend-only with local demonstration data.

IMPORTANT: This project is an educational election-system prototype. Do not claim that it is suitable for conducting legally binding public elections. A frontend-only application cannot provide secure identity verification, secret-ballot guarantees, tamper-resistant vote storage, or authoritative election results.

